risks:
Unknowns that need a paid key:
- whether BYO proxy bytes are billed;
- whether the fingerprint field is honoured;
- whether a float timeout is accepted;
- whether TIMED_OUT sessions persist Contexts;
- the never-attached session lifetime;
- fingerprint stability per Context;
- the Context size ceiling;
- which CAPTCHA vendors are covered;
- the Stagehand cache hit rate and the project flag.

recommendations:
Home a profile on Browserbase only when one of these is measured:
- a target site fails on Steel with that profile's pinned proxy and fingerprint;
- burst or pilot capacity is needed before the Steel pool exists;
- the Stagehand cache hit rate on that profile's workflows pays for the browser-hour premium.

For every Browserbase profile:
- a BYO sticky HTTP/HTTPS proxy;
- the CDP timezone override on every page;
- recordSession:false and logSession:false;
- a Context named after the profile_id with persist:true;
- a one-session-per-Context lock;
- userMetadata ownership tags;
- a fleet-held API key.

Run a paid-key validation spike on the Developer plan ($20) with public test pages only. Measure:
- BYO proxy billing;
- Context persist timing and TIMED_OUT behaviour;
- the float timeout;
- the fingerprint field;
- Live View login with keepAlive;
- the Stagehand cache HIT rate and latency.

Feed these to the Stagehand and Steel dossiers:
- the Stagehand v4 cache is Browserbase-only;
- the v4 extension must be preinstalled on remote-CDP Steel;
- browser.close() on a local-connected browser sends Browser.close.
